msgid "Filesystem operation callbacks have the signature:"
msgstr "文件系统操作回调的签名如下："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:52
msgid ""
"Let's see a simple implementation of ``cat``. We start with registering a"
" callback for when the file is opened:"
msgstr ""
"让我们来看一个 ``cat`` 的简单实现。我们先从注册一个文件打开时的回调开始："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:55
msgid "uvcat/main.c - opening a file"
msgstr "uvcat/main.c - 打开文件"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:62
msgid ""
"The ``result`` field of a ``uv_fs_t`` is the file descriptor in case of "
"the ``uv_fs_open`` callback. If the file is successfully opened, we start"
" reading it."
msgstr ""
"``result`` 字段属于 ``uv_fs_t``；在 ``uv_fs_open`` 回调的情形下，它就是文件"
"描述符。如果文件成功打开，我们就开始读取它。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:65
msgid "uvcat/main.c - read callback"
msgstr "uvcat/main.c - 读取回调"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:72
msgid ""
"In the case of a read call, you should pass an *initialized* buffer which"
" will be filled with data before the read callback is triggered. The "
"``uv_fs_*`` operations map almost directly to certain POSIX functions, so"
" EOF is indicated in this case by ``result`` being 0. In the case of "
"streams or pipes, the ``UV_EOF`` constant would have been passed as a "
"status instead."
msgstr ""
"在读取调用中，你应传入一个 *已初始化* 的缓冲区，它会在读取回调触发前被填入"
"数据。``uv_fs_*`` 操作几乎直接对应某些 POSIX 函数，因此在这种情形下，EOF "
"由 ``result`` 为 0 来表示。而在流或管道的情形下，则会以 ``UV_EOF`` 常量作"
"为状态传入。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:78
msgid ""
"Here you see a common pattern when writing asynchronous programs. The "
"``uv_fs_close()`` call is performed synchronously. *Usually tasks which "
"are one-off, or are done as part of the startup or shutdown stage are "
"performed synchronously, since we are interested in fast I/O when the "
"program is going about its primary task and dealing with multiple I/O "
"sources*. For solo tasks the performance difference usually is negligible"
" and may lead to simpler code."
msgstr ""
"这里你看到了编写异步程序时的一种常见模式。``uv_fs_close()`` 调用是同步执行"
"的。*通常，一次性的任务，或属于启动、关闭阶段一部分的任务会同步执行，因为"
"我们关心的是程序在执行主要任务、处理多个 I/O 源时的快速 I/O*。对于单独的"
"任务，性能差异通常可以忽略不计，而且这样还可能使代码更简单。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:85
msgid ""
"Filesystem writing is similarly simple using ``uv_fs_write()``.  *Your "
"callback will be triggered after the write is complete*.  In our case the"
" callback simply drives the next read. Thus read and write proceed in "
"lockstep via callbacks."
msgstr ""
"使用 ``uv_fs_write()`` 进行文件系统写入同样简单。*写入完成后，你的回调会被"
"触发*。在我们的例子中，回调只是驱动下一次读取。读和写就这样通过回调步调一"
"致地交替进行。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:90
msgid "uvcat/main.c - write callback"
msgstr "uvcat/main.c - 写入回调"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:99
msgid ""
"Due to the way filesystems and disk drives are configured for "
"performance, a write that 'succeeds' may not be committed to disk yet."
msgstr ""
"由于文件系统和磁盘驱动器为提升性能而采用的配置方式，一次“成功”的写入可能"
"尚未提交到磁盘。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:102
msgid "We set the dominos rolling in ``main()``:"
msgstr "我们在 ``main()`` 中推倒第一块多米诺骨牌："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:104
msgid "uvcat/main.c"
msgstr "uvcat/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:113
msgid ""
"The ``uv_fs_req_cleanup()`` function must always be called on filesystem "
"requests to free internal memory allocations in libuv."
msgstr ""
"必须始终对文件系统请求调用 ``uv_fs_req_cleanup()`` 函数，以释放 libuv 内部"
"的内存分配。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:117 ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:124
msgid "Filesystem operations"
msgstr "文件系统操作"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:119
msgid ""
"All the standard filesystem operations like ``unlink``, ``rmdir``, "
"``stat`` are supported asynchronously and have intuitive argument order. "
"They follow the same patterns as the read/write/open calls, returning the"
" result in the ``uv_fs_t.result`` field. The full list:"
msgstr ""
"所有标准文件系统操作（如 ``unlink``、``rmdir``、``stat``）都以异步方式受支"
"持，且参数顺序直观。它们遵循与读/写/打开调用相同的模式，在 ``uv_fs_t."
"result`` 字段中返回结果。完整列表如下："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:169
msgid "Buffers and Streams"
msgstr "缓冲区与流"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:171
msgid ""
"The basic I/O handle in libuv is the stream (``uv_stream_t``). TCP "
"sockets, TTYs, and pipes for file I/O and IPC are all treated as stream "
"subclasses."
msgstr ""
"libuv 中基本的 I/O 句柄是流（``uv_stream_t``）。TCP 套接字、TTY 以及用于文"
"件 I/O 和 IPC 的管道都被当作流的子类来对待。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:174
msgid ""
"Streams are initialized using custom functions for each subclass, then "
"operated upon using"
msgstr ""
"流使用为每个子类定制的函数进行初始化，然后使用以下函数进行操作"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:184
msgid ""
"The stream based functions are simpler to use than the filesystem ones "
"and libuv will automatically keep reading from a stream when "
"``uv_read_start()`` is called once, until ``uv_read_stop()`` is called."
msgstr ""
"基于流的函数比文件系统函数更易于使用，并且只要调用一次 ``uv_read_start()"
"``，libuv 就会自动持续从流中读取，直到调用 ``uv_read_stop()`` 为止。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:188
msgid ""
"The discrete unit of data is the buffer -- ``uv_buf_t``. This is simply a"
" collection of a pointer to bytes (``uv_buf_t.base``) and the length "
"(``uv_buf_t.len``). The ``uv_buf_t`` is lightweight and passed around by "
"value. What does require management is the actual bytes, which have to be"
" allocated and freed by the application."
msgstr ""
"数据的离散单位是缓冲区——``uv_buf_t``。它只是一组字节指针（``uv_buf_t."
"base``）与长度（``uv_buf_t.len``）的集合。``uv_buf_t`` 非常轻量，按值传递。"
"真正需要管理的是实际的字节，它们必须由应用程序来分配和释放。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:196
msgid "**THIS PROGRAM DOES NOT ALWAYS WORK, NEED SOMETHING BETTER**"
msgstr "**本程序并非总能正常工作，需要更好的方案**"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:198
msgid ""
"To demonstrate streams we will need to use ``uv_pipe_t``. This allows "
"streaming local files [#]_. Here is a simple tee utility using libuv.  "
"Doing all operations asynchronously shows the power of evented I/O. The "
"two writes won't block each other, but we have to be careful to copy over"
" the buffer data to ensure we don't free a buffer until it has been "
"written."
msgstr ""
"为了演示流，我们需要使用 ``uv_pipe_t``。它允许以流的方式处理本地文件 "
"[#]_。下面是一个使用 libuv 实现的简单 tee 工具。所有操作都以异步方式执行，"
"展现了事件驱动 I/O 的威力。两个写入不会互相阻塞，但我们必须小心地复制缓冲"
"区数据，以确保在缓冲区被写入之前不会释放它。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:204
msgid "The program is to be executed as::"
msgstr "该程序的执行方式如下："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:208
msgid ""
"We start off opening pipes on the files we require. libuv pipes to a file"
" are opened as bidirectional by default."
msgstr ""
"我们先在所需的文件上打开管道。libuv 中指向文件的管道默认以双向方式打开。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:211
msgid "uvtee/main.c - read on pipes"
msgstr "uvtee/main.c - 在管道上读取"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:218
msgid ""
"The third argument of ``uv_pipe_init()`` should be set to 1 for IPC using"
" named pipes. This is covered in :doc:`processes`. The ``uv_pipe_open()``"
" call associates the pipe with the file descriptor, in this case ``0`` "
"(standard input)."
msgstr ""
"对于使用命名管道的 IPC，``uv_pipe_init()`` 的第三个参数应设为 1。相关内容"
"在 :doc:`processes` 中有介绍。``uv_pipe_open()`` 调用将管道与文件描述符关"
"联起来，在这里是 ``0`` （标准输入）。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:223
msgid ""
"We start monitoring ``stdin``. The ``alloc_buffer`` callback is invoked "
"as new buffers are required to hold incoming data. ``read_stdin`` will be"
" called with these buffers."
msgstr ""
"我们开始监视 ``stdin``。每当需要新的缓冲区来容纳传入的数据时，就会调用 "
"``alloc_buffer`` 回调。``read_stdin`` 会带着这些缓冲区被调用。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:227
msgid "uvtee/main.c - reading buffers"
msgstr "uvtee/main.c - 读取缓冲区"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:233
msgid ""
"The standard ``malloc`` is sufficient here, but you can use any memory "
"allocation scheme. For example, node.js uses its own slab allocator which"
" associates buffers with V8 objects."
msgstr ""
"标准的 ``malloc`` 在这里就够用了，但你可以使用任何内存分配方案。例如，"
"node.js 使用自己的 slab 分配器，将缓冲区与 V8 对象关联起来。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:237
msgid ""
"The read callback ``nread`` parameter is less than 0 on any error. This "
"error might be EOF, in which case we close all the streams, using the "
"generic close function ``uv_close()`` which deals with the handle based "
"on its internal type. Otherwise ``nread`` is a non-negative number and we"
" can attempt to write that many bytes to the output streams. Finally "
"remember that buffer allocation and deallocation is application "
"responsibility, so we free the data."
msgstr ""
"读取回调的 ``nread`` 参数在发生任何错误时都小于 0。这个错误可能是 EOF，此时"
"我们会关闭所有流，使用通用的关闭函数 ``uv_close()``——它会根据句柄的内部"
"类型进行相应处理。否则 ``nread`` 是非负数，我们可以尝试将相应数量的字节写"
"入输出流。最后要记住，缓冲区的分配与释放是应用程序的责任，因此我们要释放"
"数据。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:244
msgid ""
"The allocation callback may return a buffer with length zero if it fails "
"to allocate memory. In this case, the read callback is invoked with error"
" UV_ENOBUFS. libuv will continue to attempt to read the stream though, so"
" you must explicitly call ``uv_close()`` if you want to stop when "
"allocation fails."
msgstr ""
"如果分配内存失败，分配回调可能返回长度为零的缓冲区。在这种情况下，读取回"
"调会以错误 UV_ENOBUFS 被调用。不过 libuv 仍会继续尝试读取该流，因此如果想在"
"分配失败时停止，就必须显式调用 ``uv_close()``。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:249
msgid ""
"The read callback may be called with ``nread = 0``, indicating that at "
"this point there is nothing to be read. Most applications will just "
"ignore this."
msgstr ""
"读取回调也可能以 ``nread = 0`` 被调用，表示此时没有可读的数据。大多数应用"
"程序会直接忽略这种情况。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:252
msgid "uvtee/main.c - Write to pipe"
msgstr "uvtee/main.c - 写入管道"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:258
msgid ""
"``write_data()`` makes a copy of the buffer obtained from read. This "
"buffer does not get passed through to the write callback trigged on write"
" completion. To get around this we wrap a write request and a buffer in "
"``write_req_t`` and unwrap it in the callbacks. We make a copy so we can "
"free the two buffers from the two calls to ``write_data`` independently "
"of each other. While acceptable for a demo program like this, you'll "
"probably want smarter memory management, like reference counted buffers "
"or a pool of buffers in any major application."
msgstr ""
"``write_data()`` 会复制从读取中获得的缓冲区。这个缓冲区不会被传递给写入完"
"成时触发的写入回调。为了解决这个问题，我们把一个写请求和一个缓冲区包装进 "
"``write_req_t``，并在回调中将其解包。我们进行复制，是为了能把两次 "
"``write_data`` 调用产生的两个缓冲区相互独立地释放。对于这样的演示程序来说"
"可以接受，但在任何大型应用程序中，你很可能需要更智能的内存管理，比如引用计"
"数缓冲区或缓冲区池。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:268
msgid ""
"If your program is meant to be used with other programs it may knowingly "
"or unknowingly be writing to a pipe. This makes it susceptible to "
"`aborting on receiving a SIGPIPE`_. It is a good idea to insert::"
msgstr ""
"如果你的程序会与其他程序配合使用，那么无论有意还是无意，它都可能正在向管道"
"写入。这使其面临 `aborting on receiving a SIGPIPE`_ 的风险。最好插入以下"
"内容："

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:274
msgid "in the initialization stages of your application."
msgstr "到应用程序的初始化阶段中。"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:279
msgid "File change events"
msgstr "文件变更事件"

#: ../../src/guide/filesystem.rst:281
msgid ""
"All modern operating systems provide APIs to put watches on individual "
"files or directories and be informed when the files are modified. libuv "
"wraps common file change notification libraries [#fsnotify]_. This is one"
" of the more inconsistent parts of libuv. File change notification "
"systems are themselves extremely varied across platforms so getting "
"everything working everywhere is difficult. To demonstrate, I'm going to "
"build a simple utility which runs a command whenever any of the watched "
"files change::"
msgstr ""
"所有现代操作系统都提供了对单个文件或目录设置监视并在文件被修改时获得通知的"
" API。libuv 封装了常见的文件变更通知库 [#fsnotify]_。这是 libuv 中一致性较"
"差的部分之一。文件变更通知系统本身在各平台之间差异极大，因此要让所有功能在"
"所有地方都能正常工作十分困难。为了演示，我将构建一个简单的实用工具，当任何"
"一个被监视的文件发生变化时它就会运行一条命令："

